Q10 — Secure enterprise: VLANs, DHCP, DNS, NAT, ACLs and Port Security
Example design:
VLAN 10 STAFF: 192.168.10.0/24 gateway 192.168.10.1
VLAN 20 HR:    192.168.20.0/24 gateway 192.168.20.1
VLAN 30 GUEST: 192.168.30.0/24 gateway 192.168.30.1
R1 G0/0 to SW1 trunk; R1 G0/1 to simulated ISP.
Create VLANs and access ports on switch; trunk uplink to router.

SW1:
conf t
vlan 10
 name STAFF
vlan 20
 name HR
vlan 30
 name GUEST
interface range fa0/2-5
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 10
 spanning-tree portfast
 switchport port-security
 switchport port-security maximum 2
 switchport port-security mac-address sticky
 switchport port-security violation restrict
exit
interface range fa0/6-8
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 20
 spanning-tree portfast
 switchport port-security
 switchport port-security maximum 2
 switchport port-security mac-address sticky
 switchport port-security violation restrict
exit
interface range fa0/9-10
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 30
 spanning-tree portfast
 switchport port-security
 switchport port-security maximum 2
 switchport port-security mac-address sticky
 switchport port-security violation restrict
exit
interface fa0/1
 switchport mode trunk
end
wr

R1 router-on-a-stick:
conf t
interface g0/0
 no shut
interface g0/0.10
 encapsulation dot1Q 10
 ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
 ip nat inside
interface g0/0.20
 encapsulation dot1Q 20
 ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
 ip nat inside
interface g0/0.30
 encapsulation dot1Q 30
 ip address 192.168.30.1 255.255.255.0
 ip nat inside
exit

! DHCP pools (exclude gateway addresses)
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.10.1 192.168.10.20
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.20.1 192.168.20.20
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.30.1 192.168.30.20
ip dhcp pool STAFF
 network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0
 default-router 192.168.10.1
 dns-server 8.8.8.8
ip dhcp pool HR
 network 192.168.20.0 255.255.255.0
 default-router 192.168.20.1
 dns-server 8.8.8.8
ip dhcp pool GUEST
 network 192.168.30.0 255.255.255.0
 default-router 192.168.30.1
 dns-server 8.8.8.8

! Example ACL: deny Guest VLAN access to HR VLAN, permit other IP traffic
ip access-list extended GUEST-FILTER
 deny ip 192.168.30.0 0.0.0.255 192.168.20.0 0.0.0.255
 permit ip 192.168.30.0 0.0.0.255 any
exit
interface g0/0.30
 ip access-group GUEST-FILTER in
exit

! NAT/PAT: configure G0/1 based on ISP router addressing
interface g0/1
 ip address 203.0.113.2 255.255.255.252
 ip nat outside
 no shut
exit
access-list 1 permit 192.168.10.0 0.0.0.255
access-list 1 permit 192.168.20.0 0.0.0.255
access-list 1 permit 192.168.30.0 0.0.0.255
ip nat inside source list 1 interface g0/1 overload
ip route 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 203.0.113.1
end
wr

IMPORTANT:
- Adjust interface names to your router/switch model.
- For a simulated Internet, connect an ISP router to R1 G0/1 and configure the ISP interface as 203.0.113.1/30; add an outside server/network and appropriate return routes.
- ACL above only blocks Guest-to-HR; create additional ACL entries to match your teacher's exact security policy.
- On the switch, port security requires access mode and supported switch ports. Verify with `show port-security interface fa0/2`.
- Verify VLANs: show vlan brief, show interfaces trunk.
- Verify DHCP: show ip dhcp binding.
- Verify NAT: show ip nat translations, show ip nat statistics.
- Test ping within VLANs, between VLANs, and from guest to HR (which should fail).
